---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LegalPageShell from '../../components/LegalPageShell.astro';
import { LEGAL, PRIVACY_PATH } from '../../consts';
import { recipients } from '../../data/legal';

const updated = new Date(LEGAL.privacyUpdated).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', {
  day: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  year: 'numeric',
});
---

<Layout
  path={PRIVACY_PATH}
  title="Privacy Policy - Cargo Navis"
  description="How Cargo Navis d.o.o. collects, uses and protects the personal data of website visitors and application users."
>
  <LegalPageShell heading="Privacy Policy" updatedLabel={`Last updated: ${updated}`}>
    <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
    <p>
      {LEGAL.companyName} (“Cargo Navis”, “we”) respects your privacy and is committed to protecting
      your personal data. This policy explains what data we collect through the website
      <a href="https://www.cargo-navis.com">www.cargo-navis.com</a> and the application
      <a href="https://app.cargo-navis.com">app.cargo-navis.com</a>, why we process it, who we share
      it with, and what rights you have.
    </p>
    <p>
      We process personal data in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (the General Data
      Protection Regulation, “GDPR”) and Croatian data protection legislation.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Data controller</h2>
    <p>The controller of your personal data is:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>{LEGAL.companyName}</strong></li>
      <li>Company ID (OIB): {LEGAL.oib}</li>
      <li>{LEGAL.addressLines.join(', ')}</li>
      <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.privacyEmail}`}>{LEGAL.privacyEmail}</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Definitions</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Personal data</strong> means any information relating to an identified or identifiable
      individual - for example a name, email address, phone number or IP address.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Processing</strong> means any operation performed on personal data, including
      collection, recording, storage, use, disclosure and erasure.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Data we collect</h2>

    <h3>4.1. Website visitors</h3>
    <p>
      When you visit the site, our server automatically logs technical data needed to deliver
      content and keep the service secure: IP address, browser type and version, operating system,
      date and time of the request, and the requested URL. We use no tracking cookies and no website
      analytics tools.
    </p>

    <h3>4.2. Booking a demo</h3>
    <p>
      If you book a demo through our site, the booking is handled by Google Calendar Appointment
      Schedules. You provide your name, email address and, optionally, a short note about your
      business. We use this only to arrange and hold the meeting and to follow up on your enquiry.
    </p>

    <h3>4.3. Contacting us by email</h3>
    <p>
      When you email us, we process your email address, the content of your message and any details
      you choose to send, in order to answer your enquiry.
    </p>

    <h3>4.4. Application users</h3>
    <p>
      For users of the Cargo Navis application we process account data (name, business email
      address, role), usage data, and the content users enter - such as orders, vehicles, drivers
      and documents. With respect to data our clients enter into the application, the client is the
      controller and Cargo Navis acts as a processor, working on the client's instructions under a
      data processing agreement.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Purposes and legal bases</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Delivering and securing the website</strong> - legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f)
        GDPR) in keeping the site working and protected from abuse.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Booking demos and answering enquiries</strong> - steps taken at your request prior
        to entering into a contract (Art. 6(1)(b)), or our legitimate interest in business
        communication.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Loading external content (Google Calendar)</strong> - legitimate interest (Art.
        6(1)(f) GDPR) in showing the demo booking calendar on the site.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Providing the application</strong> - performance of a contract with the client (Art.
        6(1)(b)) and compliance with legal obligations (Art. 6(1)(c)) for accounting records.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Recipients</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell personal data. We share it only with the service providers we use to run our
      service, and only to the extent necessary:
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Provider</th>
          <th>Processing location</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          recipients.map((p) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{p.name}</td>
              <td>{p.location.en}</td>
              <td>{p.purpose.en}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      We may also disclose data to competent authorities where required by law, and to our
      accounting and legal advisers, who are bound by confidentiality.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Transfers outside the EEA</h2>
    <p>
      The application database is hosted in Germany (Hetzner). Some providers - Vercel, Resend,
      Google and Meta (WhatsApp) - may process data outside the European Economic Area, primarily in
      the United States.
      Where they do, the transfer relies on the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses
      or another valid mechanism under Chapter V of the GDPR.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Retention</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Technical server logs - up to 30 days.</li>
      <li>
        Enquiry and demo correspondence - up to 24 months from the last contact, unless it leads to
        a contract.
      </li>
      <li>Account data - for the duration of the contract and 30 days after it ends.</li>
      <li>Accounting records - 11 years, as required by Croatian accounting and tax law.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
    <p>In relation to your personal data you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access</strong> - confirmation of whether we process your data, and a copy of it.</li>
      <li><strong>Rectification</strong> - correction of inaccurate or completion of incomplete data.</li>
      <li><strong>Erasure</strong> - deletion of data once it is no longer needed for these purposes.</li>
      <li><strong>Restriction of processing</strong> - in the cases set out in the GDPR.</li>
      <li><strong>Portability</strong> - receipt of your data in a structured, machine-readable format.</li>
      <li><strong>Objection</strong> - to processing based on our legitimate interest.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Withdrawal of consent</strong> - at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of
        processing before withdrawal.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Send requests to <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.privacyEmail}`}>{LEGAL.privacyEmail}</a>. We respond
      without undue delay and in any event within one month of receiving the request. Where requests
      are complex or numerous, that period may be extended by a further two months; we will tell you
      if that happens. If you believe your rights have been infringed, you may lodge
      a complaint with the Croatian Personal Data Protection Agency (AZOP),
      <a href="https://azop.hr" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">azop.hr</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Cookies and external content</h2>
    <p>
      This site uses no analytics, advertising or tracking cookies, and sets no cookies of its own.
    </p>
    <p>
      The <a href="/en/demo">Book a demo</a> page embeds Google Calendar. Opening that page loads
      the content directly from Google's servers, and Google may set its own cookies and process
      your IP address in accordance with
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Google's privacy policy
      </a>. If you would rather it did not, you can book by emailing us instead of opening that
      page.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Our services are intended for business users and are not directed at anyone under 16. We do
      not knowingly collect children's data. If we learn that we have, we delete it without delay.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Security</h2>
    <p>
      We apply appropriate technical and organisational safeguards, including encrypted transport
      (HTTPS), least-privilege access control and regular backups.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. The date of the last change is shown at the top
      of the page. We will notify users of significant changes by email or in-app notice.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For any questions about this policy or how we handle your data, contact
      <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.privacyEmail}`}>{LEGAL.privacyEmail}</a> or write to us at
      {LEGAL.addressLines.join(', ')}.
    </p>
  </LegalPageShell>
</Layout>
